    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107746" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερόπτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερόψομαι</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>contemner, disdainer,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῦ καναχῆς ὑπερόπτας</span> (dub.
			l.) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				130
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τῶν εἰωθότων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.38
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>disdainful, haughty,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς πάντα παλίγκοτος ἠδ᾽ ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.58
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. καὶ ὑβρισταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1124a29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.36J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i><i>ad Them.</i><i><span class="en">
				264d
			</span></i>.</div>
